#+TITLE: Restore CAD log before protocol termination and close the created COM instance
#+STATUS: NEXT
#+PRIORITY: P1
#+TYPE: bug
#+DEPENDS: native-cad-validation
#+BRANCH: codex/alfe-owned-shutdown
#+DATE: 2026-10-29

* Evidence
SCHME jobs succeeded while the created BricsCAD remained alive. Restart Manager
identified the surviving process holding an older job's command log. The emitted
runtime exited its SHUTDOWN loop without autolisp-finish/log restoration; killing
cscript did not close the COM application's separate process.

* Implementation
Restore settings before RESTORED, retain the exact startup COM reference, close
created documents/application, and require disappearance of PID plus creation
time. Never quit attached instances. Fail on missing cleanup acknowledgement.

* Validation
Local regression tests and the full alfe suite are being checked. Native Windows
AutoCAD/BricsCAD closure and log-release qualification remains required before
closing this issue.

Windows PowerShell validation found that the default execution policy refused
the generated helper. Version 2.3.78 supplies only a process-scoped policy and
handles a process exiting during its StartTime query; no persistent policy is
changed. Native COM qualification remains pending deployment.
